WEBVTT

00:01.920 --> 00:05.710
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.220
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.570 --> 00:15.440
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.440 --> 00:20.710
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.710 --> 00:25.290
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:26.790 --> 00:30.910
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.910 --> 00:34.100
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.610
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:11.330 --> 02:16.740
<b>Regrets Always Lie in the Past</b>

02:13.830 --> 02:16.740
Shall we begin our strategy meeting?

02:17.170 --> 02:19.860
Wethermon battle, issue number 1:

02:19.860 --> 02:22.120
Known Wethermon Info
 When the battle begins, a badstat(?) field gimmick(?)
is applied to all players.
 Levels will be reduced and equipment with level requirements 
will be force-unequippable. (Demonstrably, armor will feel
unusually heavy and hard to move in,
weapons will fly from hands.) Normal attacks can generally
be dodged by attentive players, but one hit will even kill
most tanks, so be careful!!
 Most annoying is the frequency with which he uses his
finishing move (which he always announces — telegraphing?).

How to deal with his mecha-steed remains unclear.
Slashes and magic attacks don't seem to deal damage, and if you let it be

02:20.520 --> 02:24.880
At the start of the battle, 
Wethermon activates a skill

02:24.880 --> 02:30.420
that sets the max level of all characters 
in the battle area—except for him—to 50.

02:30.420 --> 02:32.340
Max level 50?

02:32.340 --> 02:35.250
That's what you meant about our 
levels not being a problem?

02:36.490 --> 02:38.550
Wethermon's level is 200.

02:38.550 --> 02:39.850
Two hundred?!

02:38.550 --> 02:47.470
Sunraku

02:38.550 --> 02:47.470
Katzo Tataki

02:40.190 --> 02:43.510
Which means a minimum 150-level gap.

02:43.510 --> 02:46.220
That's why player skill is the key.

02:47.830 --> 02:50.950
Perfect for you, right? 
My low-level friends...

02:51.860 --> 02:55.690
You won't need to grind all 
the way to the level cap.

02:57.820 --> 02:58.690
Although...

02:59.440 --> 03:02.720
You do absolutely <i>do</i> have to reach 50.

02:59.720 --> 03:04.200
Iron Ruins of the Divinity

03:04.620 --> 03:07.200
So work hard at grinding, all right?

03:05.970 --> 03:08.450
Grinding = Repeatedly leveling up

03:09.160 --> 03:10.830
Level 50, huh?

03:11.130 --> 03:16.580
She said there was a hidden area in 
the Iron Ruins perfect for grinding,

03:16.580 --> 03:19.220
but I still gotta wonder how long it'll take.

03:19.600 --> 03:21.770
Guess we won't know until we try.

03:36.580 --> 03:38.680
It's like a whole different game in here.

03:38.680 --> 03:41.900
The black panels are sliding all around!

03:42.540 --> 03:46.870
Man, you can get do some great stuff, 
glitching out moving platforms like that.

03:47.200 --> 03:51.850
You need to soak your eyeballs and 
wash away that trash game filter, man.

03:52.370 --> 03:56.270
Hang on! I thought I'd 
experienced this vibe before!

03:56.270 --> 03:59.260
It's the final boss stage 
in <i>Brave Galaxy Fighter</i>!

03:59.260 --> 04:01.210
Never heard of that one.

04:01.210 --> 04:02.860
It's the pinnacle of sci-fi fighting games,

04:02.860 --> 04:05.760
renowned the whole world o—oh, right.

04:06.370 --> 04:09.210
Why would I know about some god-tier game?

04:09.570 --> 04:11.090
By the way, Katzo-kun.

04:11.090 --> 04:13.020
What're you up to now?

04:13.020 --> 04:14.150
Level-wise, you mean?

04:14.760 --> 04:16.150
Twenty-five.

04:16.150 --> 04:19.670
My, my! Still in your twenties, are you?

04:19.670 --> 04:20.880
So young!

04:20.880 --> 04:23.210
I happen to be 31.

04:24.380 --> 04:26.870
It's not that big a difference!

04:26.870 --> 04:31.030
He's clearly worried about how 
frail and helpless you are, Oikatzo-san!

04:31.030 --> 04:32.910
You're so wise, Emul!

04:32.910 --> 04:34.540
But I'm not!

04:34.540 --> 04:36.420
Darn it, she's got it all wrong!

04:37.450 --> 04:38.920
Sunraku-san!

04:39.620 --> 04:41.820
Something's approaching!

04:46.220 --> 04:48.680
Suppression Drone 
Type: Pyramid

04:48.970 --> 04:52.310
So there're enemies mixed in 
with the floating panels, huh?

04:52.310 --> 04:55.520
You can sit this one out, Sunraku!

04:59.530 --> 05:01.610
No matter how low your level might be...

05:02.330 --> 05:04.970
<i>SLF</i> still lets you stand a chance!

05:05.480 --> 05:07.650
You're sure we don't need to lend our aid?

05:07.650 --> 05:09.780
Eh... nah.

05:11.120 --> 05:13.320
Repel Counter!

05:14.550 --> 05:16.080
What a simple attack pattern.

05:16.080 --> 05:18.420
Wonder if you're supposed to 
practice counters on these guys.

05:19.170 --> 05:21.550
Crush Uppercut!

05:19.170 --> 05:21.550
<b><i>Crush Uppercut</i></b>

05:21.830 --> 05:23.520
Hey, one punch!

05:23.520 --> 05:25.800
You're actually quite powerful!

05:26.660 --> 05:28.990
What's with the red aura?
Some kind of buff?

05:28.610 --> 05:32.030
Buff = Enhancement

05:28.990 --> 05:30.100
Yeah.

05:30.340 --> 05:32.860
It's a spell that gives bonuses 
to strength and vitality.

05:32.860 --> 05:35.210
It's called Spirit Fist: Red.

05:33.620 --> 05:35.810
<b>Spirit Fist: Red</b>

05:40.480 --> 05:43.020
For my job, I picked a 
"spirit fist user" Monk.

05:41.840 --> 05:44.820
Job: Monk

05:43.020 --> 05:45.330
I can't equip weapons, but in exchange,

05:45.330 --> 05:47.320
I can give myself buffs and 
beat shit up with my fists!

05:47.600 --> 05:48.700
Build?

05:48.700 --> 05:51.450
Lots of HP and vitality—

05:52.150 --> 05:55.350
a light fighter, I guess you'd say!

05:56.830 --> 06:01.090
A build that assumes you'll be 
soaking lots of damage, huh?

06:01.640 --> 06:03.460
"Kill 'em before they kill you."

06:03.460 --> 06:06.590
Makes sense for a fighting gamer like you.

06:06.920 --> 06:08.160
If you're wondering, I'm—

06:08.160 --> 06:10.040
Oh, I've got you pegged already.

06:10.040 --> 06:14.350
A glass cannon with a 
strength/agility focus, right?

06:14.350 --> 06:15.740
Wrong!

06:15.740 --> 06:18.850
I'm a luck fighter, 
specializing in agility and luck!

06:20.120 --> 06:22.800
But still a glass cannon, right?

06:22.800 --> 06:25.230
He's bursting with vorpal soul!

06:25.230 --> 06:27.360
Vorpal soul?

06:27.360 --> 06:28.280
What's that?

06:28.280 --> 06:31.620
Vorpal soul is vorpal soul, of course!

06:32.990 --> 06:34.660
Let's see...

06:34.660 --> 06:38.250
Looks like the floor ahead starts 
the passage to the hidden area.

06:42.590 --> 06:46.890
Pass along the left side of 
the plate with the big hole.

06:53.370 --> 06:55.250
Jump over the fissure.

07:01.720 --> 07:04.090
Jump onto the plate with damaged sides.

07:07.580 --> 07:10.780
Slip into the crack between B2F and B3F.

07:16.910 --> 07:18.670
Now go straight.

07:23.340 --> 07:25.950
Whoever found this is something else!

07:25.950 --> 07:29.800
How do you have to be wired 
to map out a route like this?

07:30.110 --> 07:33.320
Well, Pencilgon found it, right?

07:33.320 --> 07:36.330
Seems like explanation enough to me.

07:36.330 --> 07:38.970
It truly is a maze!

07:39.180 --> 07:42.570
"Jump into the hole, and you're done," huh?

07:47.300 --> 07:49.490
It's too dark to see the bottom!

07:49.800 --> 07:54.810
Is this a weird prank to 
kill us in a roundabout way?

07:54.300 --> 07:57.220
<b>It worked!</b>

07:54.810 --> 07:56.270
No way, right?

07:57.450 --> 08:01.160
She'll have some real 
apologizing to do if so.

08:01.160 --> 08:02.500
Apologizing?!

08:02.500 --> 08:06.550
My da—er, the boss says a proper 
apology is <i>very</i> important!

08:06.550 --> 08:08.170
That's right!

08:08.640 --> 08:11.210
We dunno what's down there.

08:11.620 --> 08:16.060
I wouldn't want glass cannon Sunraku 
to get himself shattered going first.

08:17.330 --> 08:19.620
So, I'll take point!

08:19.620 --> 08:20.780
Thanks.

08:23.230 --> 08:26.170
So kind, so strong, so brave!

08:26.170 --> 08:29.060
What an admirable lady she is!

08:33.870 --> 08:35.450
That's a guy, actually.

08:36.920 --> 08:39.810
I mean, the player... Never mind.

08:39.810 --> 08:41.610
Um, point is...

08:41.610 --> 08:44.570
Sometimes a person can look like a woman, 
but they've got the soul of a man.

08:49.460 --> 08:53.180
L-Life holds so many mysteries!

08:53.180 --> 08:55.470
The world is truly vast.

08:56.070 --> 08:57.910
—ser.

08:59.930 --> 09:01.130
I think he said something.

09:01.130 --> 09:03.560
Get down here, loser!

09:03.560 --> 09:05.010
Hard to hear.

09:05.010 --> 09:07.390
Guess it's not a prank to 
get us killed, at least.

09:07.390 --> 09:10.980
"Get down here, loser!" he said.

09:13.490 --> 09:15.320
Fine, then!

09:15.320 --> 09:17.200
I'll murder that asshole!

09:17.200 --> 09:21.370
I-I'm not prepared!

09:28.610 --> 09:30.000
There you are.

09:30.280 --> 09:33.510
Surprisingly gentle slope, right?

09:36.510 --> 09:39.750
So this is the hidden 
area Pencilgon mentioned?

09:38.570 --> 09:42.010
Tearlight Lake

09:43.470 --> 09:49.020
"You can fish up a monster called the 
Lifestide Lake Serpent in the lake," it says.

09:49.320 --> 09:52.120
Apparently it gives up some sweet exp drops.

09:52.120 --> 09:54.880
Can we fish up a monster 
with these puny little rods?

09:54.880 --> 09:57.350
Well, might as well try it!

09:57.350 --> 09:58.570
Sure!

10:04.140 --> 10:07.030
Let's compete to see who 
can catch more!

10:07.030 --> 10:08.540
Got a bite already!

10:08.540 --> 10:09.610
That's fast!

10:09.960 --> 10:12.290
My father used to take 
me fishing all the time.

10:12.700 --> 10:14.600
I know all the tips and tricks.

10:14.600 --> 10:16.550
I think that's your luck stat, dude.

10:16.550 --> 10:17.920
Got me, huh?

10:22.050 --> 10:24.430
Lifestide Salmon

10:24.700 --> 10:25.890
A salmon.

10:26.610 --> 10:28.230
That's not what we're after.

10:28.230 --> 10:29.580
Looks tasty, though.

10:30.650 --> 10:31.940
Hey, I got one, too!

10:31.940 --> 10:34.000
Just another salmon, right?

10:34.570 --> 10:36.940
It looks small, so probably.

10:36.940 --> 10:38.650
Wanna try a new spot?

10:40.210 --> 10:41.620
Sunraku-san!

10:45.030 --> 10:48.210
What a grand serpent indeed!

10:50.540 --> 10:52.800
Katzo, I think that's our guy!

10:53.460 --> 10:56.300
Lifestide Lake Serpent

10:54.400 --> 10:56.870
The Lifestide Lake Serpent!

11:04.430 --> 11:08.540
Guess it's time to unveil my new weapon.

11:08.540 --> 11:09.610
Huh?

11:09.610 --> 11:13.770
I thought you were too low-level 
to equip those Moonblade things.

11:15.070 --> 11:17.540
Who ever said...

11:18.260 --> 11:20.010
I had only one weapon made?

11:20.570 --> 11:22.900
Behold, the Empire Bee Twinblades!

11:21.380 --> 11:25.490
<b>Empire Bee Twinblades
 equipped.</b>

11:22.900 --> 11:25.490
How very impressive!

11:28.080 --> 11:31.000
What, you had another new weapon?

11:31.290 --> 11:33.080
My big sister, Bee, made them!

11:33.360 --> 11:34.190
Bee?

11:44.000 --> 11:45.760
It's done!

11:45.760 --> 11:49.490
Made from the Empire Bee 
Queen material you brought...

11:49.490 --> 11:51.450
The Empire Bee Twinblades!

11:54.120 --> 11:56.400
Hey! Wake up, lazybones!

11:56.680 --> 12:01.890
What, it's done already? Um... Bilac?

12:01.890 --> 12:04.550
That's Big Sis Bee for you!

12:04.550 --> 12:07.700
You think you can disrespect 
me if Pops isn't here?!

12:07.700 --> 12:11.540
I learned the trade from him, y'know!

12:11.760 --> 12:13.970
Hey, I didn't mean it like that.

12:13.970 --> 12:15.290
I really appreciate it!

12:15.290 --> 12:19.150
I was pretty worried about what 
I'd do with my main weapon gone.

12:24.610 --> 12:29.550
Am I gonna have to manage affection levels 
with rabbits other than Emul and Vash?

12:30.260 --> 12:32.280
It's not a dang dating sim!

12:33.180 --> 12:34.260
Actually...

12:34.260 --> 12:37.130
The thought of having to 
manage affection levels with

12:37.130 --> 12:40.820
more rabbits in the future makes me...

12:42.220 --> 12:44.380
What's the matter, Sunraku-san?

12:46.510 --> 12:50.080
I'm getting trauma flashbacks 
from that trash game dating sim!

12:51.050 --> 12:56.490
I once had to balance affection levels 
between twelve girls without a moment's slip.

12:57.010 --> 12:58.870
The slightest lapse in attention

12:58.870 --> 13:02.090
would trigger a domino effect 
of tumbling affection levels...

13:02.740 --> 13:05.440
And I'd land the bad end where all the girls

13:05.440 --> 13:08.330
move to Italy to apprentice at a pizzeria!

13:10.110 --> 13:12.390
The heck're you talking about?

13:12.390 --> 13:16.250
Sunraku Picklefish's adolescence, 
crushed beneath a pizza stone.

13:17.790 --> 13:20.360
But hey, look at these new weapons!

13:20.360 --> 13:23.250
Empire Bee Twinblades, huh?

13:25.280 --> 13:27.360
You're pretty good.

13:27.360 --> 13:28.640
Damn right I am.

13:28.640 --> 13:30.620
It's very impressive indeed!

13:30.620 --> 13:36.100
Glad I came back for the Queen's 
materials after I beat the Quad Beetle.

13:36.100 --> 13:38.060
Those blades'll serve you well.

13:38.520 --> 13:41.500
The right-hand blade has a special attribute.

13:41.850 --> 13:43.020
The right-hand...?

13:45.570 --> 13:47.380
<b>Spiral Edge</b>

13:52.850 --> 13:54.390
This thing is too damn tough!

13:54.730 --> 13:58.650
We're too low-level to put 
more than a scratch on it!

14:01.210 --> 14:05.150
<i>Some weapons, skills, spells, 
and monster attacks</i>

14:06.230 --> 14:11.390
<i>have the "corrode" attribute, 
which destroys part of an avatar itself.</i>

14:11.860 --> 14:15.800
<i>If you deal enough damage to 
the part you want to take out,</i>

14:16.130 --> 14:20.380
<i>it'll cause visible damage to the part in 
question and create a weak point there.</i>

14:20.920 --> 14:26.050
But that weapon doesn't 
corrode in the normal way.

14:26.970 --> 14:30.430
It infects the part you attack 
and corrodes it over time—

14:30.430 --> 14:31.880
with corrosive poison.

14:30.530 --> 14:32.640
Corrosive Poison

14:35.100 --> 14:36.660
<i>It acts like poison—</i>

14:36.660 --> 14:40.350
<i>the "corrode" attribute building up and 
worming its way in little by little.</i>

14:41.040 --> 14:43.730
<i>And if you keep dealing more corrosive 
poison with repeated strikes...</i>

14:44.080 --> 14:46.280
<i>it breaks through the 
enemy's debuff resistance</i>

14:46.280 --> 14:48.740
<i>and causes the corrode attribute 
to show itself faster!</i>

14:48.970 --> 14:50.740
I've stripped away its scales, Katzo!

14:50.740 --> 14:51.650
Got it!

14:51.650 --> 14:52.870
I'll bring out the big guns!

14:53.080 --> 14:55.620
Spirit Fist: Black!

15:05.700 --> 15:06.710
Nice!

15:06.710 --> 15:09.050
It's a proper weak point now.

15:10.070 --> 15:12.760
I-I'll aid in the fight!

15:14.510 --> 15:15.510
Emul!

15:21.210 --> 15:22.190
Katzo!

15:23.270 --> 15:25.690
I built myself to tank damage, remember?

15:25.690 --> 15:27.590
That won't be enough to take me out!

15:27.590 --> 15:30.200
Th-Thank you so much!

15:32.870 --> 15:34.870
Repel Counter!

15:34.870 --> 15:37.370
Nice stun! Now, let's press the attack!

15:37.370 --> 15:38.010
Yeah!

15:38.010 --> 15:39.120
Indeed!

15:39.330 --> 15:41.720
I'll cut you into serpent fillets!

15:39.330 --> 15:41.720
I'll make minced eel out of you!

15:39.330 --> 15:41.720
Take this! Magic Edge!

15:47.460 --> 15:48.970
Hell yeah!

15:48.970 --> 15:50.470
We defeated it!

15:50.470 --> 15:51.970
Nice work!

15:58.260 --> 16:00.640
Hey, I leveled up already!

16:00.640 --> 16:03.290
These guys really do offer 
great exp for the effort.

16:03.290 --> 16:05.530
Boy, that thing was tough.

16:05.530 --> 16:07.970
I got a four-level jump!

16:08.660 --> 16:10.650
Hey, I learned new skills, too!

16:11.290 --> 16:14.410
Wonder if I can link 'em 
at the Skill Garden...

16:15.420 --> 16:19.430
Linking skills? You thinking 
of another game again?

16:25.420 --> 16:26.570
No, man!

16:26.570 --> 16:28.460
<i>SLF</i> is a game about skills.

16:28.460 --> 16:33.740
Of course you can combine the ones you 
learn to create combo skills, right?

16:33.740 --> 16:34.820
Combine?

16:33.740 --> 16:38.320
Combine...

16:34.820 --> 16:38.760
Remember the tutorial in Firstia, 
the starting town?!

16:38.760 --> 16:41.110
Firstia? Never went.

16:42.930 --> 16:48.190
Fighter-type Skill
Power Direct Lv. 5

16:42.930 --> 16:48.190
Critical-enhancement Skill
Critical Assist Lv. 3

16:43.370 --> 16:45.810
Skills with proficiency 
levels can be linked up

16:45.810 --> 16:49.180
at a facility called the Skill Garden.

16:48.190 --> 16:50.210
<b>Link</b>

16:49.670 --> 16:53.320
That lets you create new "combo skills"!

16:50.210 --> 16:53.320
Chance of KO effect
on critical hit
<b>Knockout</b>

16:53.770 --> 16:56.090
P-Proficiency levels?!

16:55.680 --> 17:10.000
Repel Counter
 Flash Counter
 Loop Slash <b>Lv.5
</b>Accel <b>LV.6</b>

16:56.710 --> 16:58.030
That's right...

16:58.030 --> 17:00.500
I was wondering why some 
skills changed their name,

17:00.500 --> 17:02.150
like Repel Counter to Flash Counter,

17:02.150 --> 17:06.410
and some just came with 
level numbers to raise...

17:06.800 --> 17:10.000
So the second kind can be linked up?!

17:10.290 --> 17:13.620
You can also go to the 
Skill Garden to find out how long until

17:13.620 --> 17:15.240
your skills level up or evolve,

17:15.240 --> 17:18.110
and find out conditions 
for learning new skills.

17:18.110 --> 17:19.470
It's pretty crucial stuff!

17:19.470 --> 17:21.680
They also sell grimoires there, and—

17:24.170 --> 17:26.840
Sunraku-san! Are you all right?

17:27.290 --> 17:31.320
Don't tell me... you don't even 
know about sub-jobs and guilds?

17:28.620 --> 17:30.880
Sub-jobs

17:29.380 --> 17:30.880
Guilds

17:33.090 --> 17:38.000
How much did I miss by 
skipping one little town?!

17:39.370 --> 17:41.020
Fine, whatever!

17:41.020 --> 17:44.180
Wallowing in regret will 
just get me depressed!

17:44.180 --> 17:46.590
Let's get back to the grind!

17:52.200 --> 17:55.460
The best cure for bad 
memories is simple labor!

17:55.790 --> 17:59.320
Let's catch us a big eel, Katzo! Emul!

17:59.320 --> 18:01.140
R-Righty-o!

18:02.300 --> 18:04.690
Going for the mental blackout, huh?

18:09.270 --> 18:13.020
<b>Oikatzo</b>

18:09.270 --> 18:13.020
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

18:09.700 --> 18:13.020
Level 42 and Level 40?

18:13.020 --> 18:16.510
That's a lot of progress 
in pretty a short time.

18:16.510 --> 18:18.990
You could even afford to slow down a bit...

18:18.990 --> 18:19.980
What got into you?

18:19.980 --> 18:24.060
Actually, turns out Sunraku 
skipped the tutori—

18:24.920 --> 18:27.610
Fine, fine. I won't tell her.

18:28.730 --> 18:33.970
Still, Emul-chan's got some 
pretty nice attack power!

18:35.110 --> 18:37.200
I'm truly exhausted!

18:37.200 --> 18:40.600
It just so happens, 
my dear little Emul is level 56!

18:41.930 --> 18:44.680
And this tent's a handy little thing, huh?

18:44.680 --> 18:48.200
It's not the coziest, but it
lets you make a save point, right?

18:44.680 --> 18:53.940
<b>Save Tent</b>

18:48.200 --> 18:50.180
Yeah, but they're the worst.

18:50.180 --> 18:53.940
Stupidly expensive for something 
with a limited number of uses.

18:54.250 --> 18:58.950
I'd never use one for this if 
we weren't pressed for time.

18:59.450 --> 19:02.760
Well, enough sitting around. Let's go!

19:02.760 --> 19:03.780
Go?

19:03.780 --> 19:04.950
Go where?

19:06.370 --> 19:10.150
It's a full moon tonight. 
The only time we can meet her.

19:12.170 --> 19:13.490
Meet who?

19:14.370 --> 19:19.280
In order to fight Wethermon the Tombguard, 
there's someone we need to talk to.

19:21.060 --> 19:25.570
The unique NPC... Setsuna of Bygone Days.

19:27.170 --> 19:28.410
Set-chan.

19:29.630 --> 19:44.130
<i>Into the gap between moments</i>

19:46.150 --> 19:55.690
<i>spills a single wish</i>

21:35.940 --> 21:43.200
<b>SLF Mini</b>

21:36.630 --> 21:40.450
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

21:39.750 --> 21:43.200
<i><b>Animalia Expedition ~ Monster-Bird of
the Forest Grotto
 The "Rabbit-Eared Shoebill" Really Exists!</b></i>

21:40.450 --> 21:41.970
Mini!

21:43.200 --> 23:03.280
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

21:44.150 --> 21:46.640
<i>The Prismatic Forest Grotto—</i>

21:46.640 --> 21:51.200
<i>Within it is a legend, 
spoken of only in whispers.</i>

21:53.320 --> 21:55.170
<i>The mysterious monster-bird,</i>

21:55.170 --> 21:56.810
<i>the Rabbit-Eared Shoebill!</i>

21:57.120 --> 22:00.710
<i>Does this legendary bird really exist?!</i>

22:00.980 --> 22:04.110
<b>Animalia Expedition</b>

22:04.610 --> 22:07.650
<b>Monster-Bird of the Forest Grotto</b>

22:07.650 --> 22:11.490
<b>The "Rabbit-Eared Shoebill"
Really Exists</b>

22:11.600 --> 22:14.510
The mysterious monster-bird...

22:15.210 --> 22:20.330
We'll use all of SF-Zoo's animal 
knowledge to find it, or die trying!

22:20.330 --> 22:22.680
Captain! Look at this!

22:25.950 --> 22:29.900
Is this... a footprint from 
the Rabbit-Eared Shoebill?

22:29.900 --> 22:32.280
Looks more humanoid than bird-like...

22:33.120 --> 22:37.500
<i>Following the footsteps, 
the expedition moved further into the forest.</i>

22:38.240 --> 22:40.040
<i>And that's when they heard it!</i>

22:44.050 --> 22:46.100
Captain! That call...

22:46.100 --> 22:49.380
It must be the Rabbit-Eared Shoebill!

22:49.590 --> 22:53.110
<i>The piercing call caused 
them to tremble in fear!</i>

22:53.110 --> 22:55.000
<i>And then they saw it!</i>

23:01.010 --> 23:01.920
We found it!

23:01.920 --> 23:02.790
Let's chase it down!

23:02.790 --> 23:03.560
Right!

23:06.430 --> 23:10.340
<i>They were unable to get 
a clear image on camera.</i>

23:10.880 --> 23:14.330
<i>But the Rabbit-Eared 
Shoebill truly did exist!</i>

23:15.450 --> 23:17.420
<i>Their desperate search proved in vain,</i>

23:17.420 --> 23:20.830
<i>and they were unable to 
get a clear shot of it.</i>

23:22.230 --> 23:26.340
<i>Nevertheless, the Animalia 
Expedition's search continued.</i>

23:26.990 --> 23:30.870
<i>Some day, they would find 
that mysterious animal!</i>

23:34.690 --> 23:41.020
Man, watching that huge beetle send 
you flying was hilarious, Sunraku.

23:41.020 --> 23:43.890
I'm just glad I survived.

23:43.890 --> 23:47.320
I'm still not sure that I did!
